messages:
Maya: Quick pass on dark-mode hover states for token chips in the dashboard. Current hover feels too bright against the terminal panel — wondering about dialing it back. Thoughts?
Jules: Agreed, it pops too much. My take: lower saturation and nudge hover darker, keep a subtle focus ring for keyboard users. Proposal: --token-bg: #0f1113; hover: #16181a; focus-ring: rgba(255,255,255,0.06).
Ravi: Can you paste a tiny snippet so frontend can try? :eyes:
Jules: ```css
:root[data-theme='dark'] {
  --token-bg: #0f1113;
  --token-hover: #16181a;
  --token-focus-ring: rgba(255,255,255,0.08);
}
.token { background: var(--token-bg); }
.token:hover { background: var(--token-hover); }
.token:focus-visible { box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px var(--token-focus-ring); }
```
Maya: That helps. Two quick nits: hover still reads low-contrast at 14px — can we try `--token-hover: #1e2226`? Also focus ring should remain visible when charts are behind the tokens.
Nikhil: For charts — stacked area colors lose distinction at 40% opacity on dark bg. Suggest shifting mid-tones warmer and offering patterned fills as an accessibility fallback.
Sam: Patterned fills could be optional. UX question: add toggle in Accessibility settings to enable 'patterned charts'?
Maya: Yes to a toggle. Default: solid colors, auto-enable patterns when OS high-contrast is on or when we detect low series contrast.
Jules: Implementation idea: detect contrast ratio < 3:1 for series colors, then overlay SVG patterns. Use `mix-blend-mode: screen` for legibility.
Ravi: Quick impl note: `fill: url(#hatch-1)` as fallback, and keep color fill for users without pattern support.
Sam: Copy tweak for the toggle label: my first draft "Chart accessibility: patterns for colorblind / low-contrast" — seems long. Suggestions?
Maya: Prefer something concise: "Accessible chart patterns" plus a tooltip: "Use patterns to help distinguish series when color contrast is low."
design-bot: New design tokens added: --token-hover-2: #1e2226, --chart-patterns-enabled: false (staging).
Nikhil: Quick contrast check request: with hover #1e2226, white text @14px — does that hit 4.5:1? Can someone run axe or Lighthouse?
Jules: I'll run the a11y checks and post screenshots tomorrow. @Maya can we test on the beta branch once deployed?
deploy-bot: deploy started — branch=design/dark-token-hover job=ci-frontend-045
Maya: Thanks — will test post-deploy and report back. :thumbsup:
